        "title": "Stability and Linearization",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The central engine of the whole subject: to decide whether a fixed point is stable, **linearize**\nthe flow around it and read the **eigenvalues of the Jacobian**. The signs of their real parts\nsettle the question for hyperbolic fixed points (Hartman–Grobman). When eigenvalues sit on the\nimaginary axis, linearization fails and you reach for a **Lyapunov function**. This chapter is the\nlinear-algebra core; Chapter 03 studies what happens *at* the failure boundary."
    }
